-- ugcportal-hx2: a structured basis for a MUSIC clearance.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-migrations prisma/migrations
-- --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script`; the comments are the only
-- hand-edit.
--
-- TWO NULLABLE COLUMNS, NO DEFAULT, NOTHING BACKFILLED. `basis` holds a
-- ClearanceBasis value (SQLite stores a Prisma enum as TEXT; the generated
-- client is what restricts it to LICENCE / ORIGINAL_SCORE / MUTED_DELIVERY),
-- and `basisEvidence` the licence's evidence reference when basis is LICENCE.
-- A MUSIC clearance written before this ran therefore has basis NULL, and the
-- gate (layerIsCleared in src/lib/resale-rights.ts) no longer counts it as
-- cleared: a free-text reason is not a stated ground, and "deliver it muted"
-- is not one while the sold file is the raw original. That is the fail-closed
-- direction on purpose, and there is no production data to re-record. Every
-- other layer's rows keep basis NULL, which is what they are required to
-- carry.
--
-- AN `ADD COLUMN`, NOT A TABLE REBUILD, for the reason 20261017120000 gives:
-- it composes with any other bead adding a column to the same table. The
-- rules about which basis is allowed on which layer live in the one writer
-- (src/lib/curation-clearance-write.ts), not in a CHECK constraint, so a
-- refusal reaches the admin as a sentence rather than as a driver error.
--
-- DEPLOY ORDER: apply before the new build. A new build against an
-- un-migrated database fails every MediaRightsClearance read (the generated
-- client selects the new columns); an old build against a migrated database
-- ignores them.

-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "MediaRightsClearance" ADD COLUMN "basis" TEXT;
ALTER TABLE "MediaRightsClearance" ADD COLUMN "basisEvidence" TEXT;
